{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Passwordless Multi-Auth API",
    "description": "Passwordless Multi-Auth Platform API - Passwordless Authentication\n\nThis API provides comprehensive endpoints for:\n- MagicLink-based passwordless authentication\n- User management and security operations\n- Role and authority management\n- Push notifications\n- TOTP/MFA verification\n\n## Authentication Flow\n1. Call `POST /api/auth/email-magiclink/send` with user email\n2. User opens the emailed link in a browser: `GET /api/auth/verify?token={token}`\n3. The server redirects (302) to the app scheme `passwordless://auth/callback?code={code}` (or `?status=totp_required` when MFA is enabled, `?status=error&reason=...` on failure)\n4. Trade the one-time code for a token pair via `POST /api/auth/exchange` (if TOTP was required, call `POST /api/auth/totp/verify` instead)\n5. Use the returned JWT in the Authorization header: `Bearer {token}`\n6. Renew with `POST /api/auth/refresh` (single-use rotation); revoke with `POST /api/auth/logout`\n\n## Flutter Integration\nFor Flutter apps, use the `/api/auth/email-magiclink/send` endpoint\nfor mobile authentication. The MagicLink can be handled via\ndeep linking in your Flutter app.\n",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Passwordless Multi-Auth Team",
      "email": "api@example.com"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "Private",
      "url": "https://github.com/ersincivi/spring-boot-passwordless-multi-auth"
    },
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:8080",
      "description": "Local Development"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://api.example.com",
      "description": "Production"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
